+<h3 id="evidence-tiers-and-actual-execution">Evidence tiers and actual execution</h3>
+<p>ArduPilot Copter-4.7.2 runs native autopilot software against its simulated flight dynamics. Commands pass through SwarmKit's production MAVLink backend. Each flight owns its process, parameters and isolated localhost ports; no physical aircraft was connected. The final protocol assigns <strong>24 flights: six conditions × two policies × two noise seeds</strong>. This is a small integration qualification, not a powered effectiveness comparison.</p>
+<p><strong>Native MAVLink</strong> preserves backend-specific accuracy semantics. Those fields do not become deterministic hard bounds; unverified arrival and coverage must remain unfulfilled even when the vehicle reaches B. <strong>Synthetic bounded observations</strong> use an explicitly named test adapter, perturbed simulator position and an ideal flat nadir camera. Raw SIM_STATE is recorded independently. Production MAVLink recovery stays disabled.</p>
+<p>SITL qualification is in progress; no final measurement is asserted here.</p>
 
